        {
          "body": "[P1] Bound decompression output before decoding\n\nA small compressed response can expand far beyond `MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES` inside `decoder.decode(chunk)` before the decoded-size check runs, potentially allocating enough memory to exhaust the capture worker. Enforce an output limit during incremental decompression, rather than only checking the returned bytes afterward.",
          "commit_id": "90ff83f6559786307478ff3e117d3197cfbd9155",
          "created_at": "2026-10-09T19:56:00Z",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/magnus919/SlopSearX/pull/742#discussion_r4234035748",
          "id": 4234035748,
          "line": null,
          "original_commit_id": "90ff83f6559786307478ff3e117d3197cfbd9155",
          "original_line": 516,
          "original_start_line": null,
          "path": "scripts/coverage_source_capture.py",
          "pull_request_review_id": 5474752584,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "start_line": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-09T19:56:00Z",
          "user": {
            "id": 138933559,
            "login": "factory-droid[bot]",
            "type": "Bot"
          }
        },
        {
          "body": "[P1] Decode buffered responses before credential screening\n\n`Response(content=..., headers={\"Content-Encoding\": \"gzip\"})` is marked stream-consumed by HTTPX, but its `_content` still contains the encoded bytes. Treating `response.content` as already decoded means the credential scan examines compressed data and misses a reflected operator token; the replacement response retains the encoding header, so HTTPX decodes it for the caller and the reflected token can be written into a saved context. Decode buffered content according to its `Content-Encoding` before scanning, or reject such responses.",
          "commit_id": "90ff83f6559786307478ff3e117d3197cfbd9155",
          "created_at": "2026-10-09T19:56:00Z",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/magnus919/SlopSearX/pull/742#discussion_r4234035758",
